Changelog: 04-11-2026 19:05:17

Added. run.ps1 starts Nexus Installer Tests on Windows with the checkout's Windows venv, as run.sh does on Linux,
so Nexus Dashboard's tile for it is on there too and opens it on the suite chosen there (--suite NAME). The
runner's PATH test uses this system's path separator.

Changelog: 02-11-2026 00:49:20

Added. Nexus Installer Tests, a Nexus app in dev/itests/ (owner, 02-11-2026: the tools for working on the suites
are Nexus's, in one place): BC-250 Installer Tests moved out of the BC250 Bazzite Suite (tools/installer-tests/gui)
and made every suite's. The header's Suite box lists the suites of the checkout whose installer tests run on this
system, a Bazzite suite's .sh tests on Linux (bash, with fakeroot) and a Windows suite's .ps1 tests on Windows
(PowerShell), and remembers the choice (--suite NAME opens one). It runs from the checkout with the dev venv
(run.sh, bc250_core from core/: its own copies of instance.py and theme.py are gone), takes Nexus's design and
icon (core's nexus.py; the development category icon it had is gone), and is never released (.checkout-only).
install.sh writes the launcher, menu entry and Desktop icon for this checkout, and removes the earlier name's.
Breaking. The app id is nexus-installer-tests (it was bc250-installer-test-gui) and the package installer_tests;
the version stays 0.1.0 until the owner bumps it.

